","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata, collections\n\ndef deacc(s):\n    return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\ndef norm(s):\n    s = deacc(s).lower()\n    s = re.sub(r'\\(.*?\\)', ' ', s)          # drop parentheticals\n    s = re.sub(r'\\s*-\\s*([a-z]{2})$', '', s) # trailing -UF\n    s = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', ' ', s)\n    return ' '.join(s.split())\n\np='data/kaggle/'\nallteams = collections.Counter()\nfor fn, cols in [('Brasileirao_Matches.csv',('home_team','away_team')),\n                 ('Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv',('home_team','away_team')),\n                 ('Libertadores_Matches.csv',('home_team','away_team')),\n                 ('BR-Football-Dataset.csv',('home','away'))]:\n    with open(p+fn, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols: allteams[norm(r[c])] += 1\nwith open(p+'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        allteams[norm(r['Equipe_mandante'])] += 1\n        allteams[norm(r['Equipe_visitante'])] += 1\nprint(\"distinct normalized:\", len(allteams))\n# Show groups that might need merging: focus on big Brazilian clubs\nfor k in sorted(allteams):\n    if any(t in k for t in ['palmeiras','flamengo','corinthians','sao paulo','santos','gremio','cruzeiro','atletico','athletico','internacional','vasco','botafogo','fluminense','bahia','sport','vitoria','ceara','fortaleza','goias','parana','chapecoense','avai','ponte preta','america','bragantino','gremio']):\n        print(f\"{allteams[k]:5d}  {k}\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788239343255,"end":1788239343257}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good. The FIFA dataset has Brazilian clubs like Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Santos, Internacional, Botafogo, Bahia, Paraná, Atlético Paranaense, Chapecoense, Ceará Sporting Club, Sport Club do Recife, Vitória, América FC (Minas Gerais). Note \"Atlético Madrid\" is Spanish. So fuzzy club matching needs care — I need a club-normalization that maps Brazilian club name variants.\n\nAlso note: my keyword search caught some false positives (\"Atlético Madrid\", \"Sporting CP\", etc. are not Brazilian). For \"players at Brazilian clubs\" queries, I should have a curated mapping of well-known Brazilian clubs to their FIFA club-name variants, and match exactly on normalized forms.\n\nKey mapping challenges for clubs:\n- FIFA: \"Atlético Mineiro\" vs match data \"Atletico-MG\"/\"Atlético-MG\"/\"Atlético Mineiro\"?\n- FIFA: \"Atlético Paranaense\" vs \"Athletico-PR\"/\"Atletico-PR\"\n- FIFA: \"Ceará Sporting Club\" vs \"Ceara-CE\"\n- FIFA: \"Sport Club do Recife\" vs \"Sport-PE\"\n- FIFA: \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" vs \"América-MG\"/\"America-MG\"\n- FIFA: \"Grêmio\" vs \"Grêmio\"/\"Gremio\"\n- FIFA: \"Vitória\" vs \"Vitória-BA\" (but also \"Vitória Guimarães\" is Portuguese — exact match \"Vitória\" is fine)\n- FIFA: \"Santos\" vs \"Santos-SP\" (but \"Santos Laguna\" is Mexican — exact match fine)\n- FIFA: \"Bahia\" vs \"Bahia-BA\"\n- FIFA: \"Paraná\" vs \"Paraná-PR\"/\"Parana-PR\"/\"Paraná Clube\"\n- FIFA: \"Botafogo\" vs \"Botafogo-RJ\" (also \"Botafogo PB\"? Not in FIFA 19 I think)\n- FIFA: \"Fluminense\" vs \"Fluminense-RJ\"\n- FIFA: \"Cruzeiro\" vs \"Cruzeiro-MG\"\n- FIFA: \"Internacional\" vs \"Internacional-RS\"\n- FIFA: \"Chapecoense\" vs \"Chapecoense-SC\"\n\nNow team name normalization across match files:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"America-MG\", \"Atletico-MG\", \"Avai-SC\", \"Sport-PE\", \"Atletico-PR\", \"Athletico-PR\"? Let me check whether it uses \"Athletico\" or \"Atletico\". From the sample: 'Atletico-PR'. And novo uses \"Athletico-PR\". FIFA uses \"Atlético Paranaense\". Also \"São Paulo\"? Let me check the Brasileirao team list fully. Also BR-Football uses \"Sao Paulo\" (no accents).\n\n- Brazilian_Cup: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\" (space around dash), \"Abc - RN\".\n\n- Libertadores: \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Boca Juniors\" — foreign teams with country qualifiers in parens.\n\n- novo: \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"Goiás\", \"Criciúma\".\n\n- BR-Football: \"Sao Paulo\" — de-accented.\n\nNormalization strategy:\n1. Unicode NFKD → strip accents/diacritics → ASCII.\n2. Lowercase.\n3. Remove state suffixes: strip trailing \"-sp\", \"-rj\", \"-mg\", etc. (2-letter UF codes), and \" - rj\" variants.\n4. Remove parenthetical qualifiers: \"(urU)\", \"(antigo ...)\".\n5. Remove common corporate/legal suffixes: \"sport club\", \"clube\", \"esporte clube\", \"fc\", \"sc\"? Careful — \"Sport Club do Recife\" → strip \"sport club\"? That would leave \"recife\". Hmm, \"Sport\" is itself a team (\"Sport-PE\" → \"sport\"). \"Sport Club do Recife\" normalized → \"sport club do recife\" — need alias mapping for that.\n\nThe cleanest robust approach: canonical-name registry + alias table with hand-curated entries for all teams appearing in the datasets (there are maybe 100-200 Brazilian teams), plus generic algorithmic normalization as fallback. Let me count distinct teams per file to see how big the curation needs to be.\n\nActually, a hybrid: \n- `normalize_team(name)`: algorithmic (deaccent, lowercase, remove parentheses, remove state suffix, strip punctuation, collapse spaces) → produces a normalized key.\n- Alias table mapping known variants to canonical display names (e.g., \"atletico paranaense\", \"athletico pr\", → \"Athletico-PR\"; \"ceara sporting club\" → \"Ceará\"; \"sport club do recife\" → \"Sport\").\n\nLet me enumerate distinct teams across files to design the alias","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b5ee26b001zoWwaJJO00Z8AU","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b5eba360011PtOow8C8UvvRX"}}
