{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239505738,"sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8bda1f11b6e3df44","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nsa = [r for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A']\nper = collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in sa)\nprint(\"BRF Serie A per year:\", dict(sorted(per.items())))\ncd = [r for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil']\nprint(\"BRF Cup per year:\", dict(sorted(collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in cd).items())))\nsb = collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie B')\nprint(\"BRF Serie B per year:\", dict(sorted(sb.items())))\n# 2023 Serie A standings quick check\npts=collections.defaultdict(lambda: [0,0,0,0,0,0])  # W D L GF GA pts\nfor r in sa:\n    if not r['date'].startswith('2023'): continue\n    hg, ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n    h,a = r['home'], r['away']\n    for t,gf,ga in ((h,hg,ag),(a,ag,hg)):\n        rec=pts[t]\n        rec[3]+=gf; rec[4]+=ga\n        if gf>ga: rec[0]+=1; rec[5]+=3\n        elif gf==ga: rec[1]+=1; rec[5]+=1\n        else: rec[2]+=1\ntop=sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1][5])[:5]\nfor t,(w,d,l,gf,ga,s) in top: print(f\"  {t}: {s} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L)\")\nprint(\"total 2023 SA matches:\", sum(1 for r in sa if r['date'].startswith('2023')))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-8c2c162e81b7"},"output":"BRF Serie A per year: {'2014': 281, '2015': 378, '2016': 379, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 264, '2021': 491, '2022': 379, '2023': 377}\nBRF Cup per year: {'2014': 43, '2015': 139, '2016': 147, '2017': 105, '2018': 111, '2019': 117, '2020': 117, '2021': 111, '2022': 117, '2023': 116}\nBRF Serie B per year: {'2014': 275, '2015': 378, '2016': 380, '2017': 381, '2018': 377, '2019': 378, '2020': 302, '2021': 446, '2022': 380, '2023': 380}\n  Gremio: 68 pts (21W 5D 12L)\n  Palmeiras: 67 pts (19W 10D 8L)\n  Flamengo: 66 pts (19W 9D 10L)\n  Atletico Mineiro: 66 pts (19W 9D 10L)\n  Botafogo RJ: 64 pts (18W 10D 10L)\ntotal 2023 SA matches: 377\n","metadata":{"output":"BRF Serie A per year: {'2014': 281, '2015': 378, '2016': 379, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 264, '2021': 491, '2022': 379, '2023': 377}\nBRF Cup per year: {'2014': 43, '2015': 139, '2016': 147, '2017': 105, '2018': 111, '2019': 117, '2020': 117, '2021': 111, '2022': 117, '2023': 116}\nBRF Serie B per year: {'2014': 275, '2015': 378, '2016': 380, '2017': 381, '2018': 377, '2019': 378, '2020': 302, '2021': 446, '2022': 380, '2023': 380}\n  Gremio: 68 pts (21W 5D 12L)\n  Palmeiras: 67 pts (19W 10D 8L)\n  Flamengo: 66 pts (19W 9D 10L)\n  Atletico Mineiro: 66 pts (19W 9D 10L)\n  Botafogo RJ: 64 pts (18W 10D 10L)\ntotal 2023 SA matches: 377\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nsa = [r for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie A']\nper = collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in sa)\nprint(\"BRF Serie A per year:\", dict(sorted(per.items())))\ncd = [r for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Copa do Brasil']\nprint(\"BRF Cup per year:\", dict(sorted(collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in cd).items())))\nsb = collections.Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in rows if r['tournament']=='Serie B')\nprint(\"BRF Serie B per year:\", dict(sorted(sb.items())))\n# 2023 Serie A standings quick check\npts=collections.defaultdict(lambda: [0,0,0,0,0,0])  # W D L GF GA pts\nfor r in sa:\n    if not r['date'].startswith('2023'): continue\n    hg, ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n    h,a = r['home'], r['away']\n    for t,gf,ga in ((h,hg,ag),(a,ag,hg)):\n        rec=pts[t]\n        rec[3]+=gf; rec[4]+=ga\n        if gf>ga: rec[0]+=1; rec[5]+=3\n        elif gf==ga: rec[1]+=1; rec[5]+=1\n        else: rec[2]+=1\ntop=sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1][5])[:5]\nfor t,(w,d,l,gf,ga,s) in top: print(f\"  {t}: {s} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L)\")\nprint(\"total 2023 SA matches:\", sum(1 for r in sa if r['date'].startswith('2023')))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788239505733,"end":1788239505736}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed: FIFA 19 dataset here does NOT include Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Vasco, Grêmio is there (\"Grêmio\" was in br list and True). So Brazilian clubs in FIFA data: Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Santos, Internacional, América FC (Minas Gerais), Botafogo, Bahia, Paraná, Atlético Paranaense, Vitória, Sport Club do Recife, Chapecoense, Ceará Sporting Club (15 clubs × 20 Brazilian players = 300 players + Brazilian players abroad).\n\nThe spec example \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" — the answer will be \"no Flamengo players in the FIFA dataset\" (the dataset has a licensing gap). My tools must handle this gracefully and the README should document it. Also \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" → honest empty result with an explanatory note. That's fine — it's what the data supports. I could ALSO answer \"players AT the club in match data\" — no player names in match data. So empty + note.\n\nNow — the club registry. Let me now design it completely. I'll write a curated registry in `soccer_mcp/clubs.py`:\n\n```python\nCLUBS = [\n    Club(id=\"flamengo\", name=\"Flamengo\", state=\"RJ\", country=\"BRA\",\n         aliases={\"flamengo\", \"flamengo rj\", \"cr flamengo\", ...}),\n    ...\n]\n```\n\nCanonical clubs to curate (from cross-file + major clubs):\n\nSerie A regulars (Brasileirao file): America-MG, Atletico-GO, Atletico-MG, Atletico-PR(Athletico), Avai, Bahia, Botafogo-RJ, Ceara, Chapecoense, Corinthians, Coritiba, Criciuma, CSA, Cruzeiro, Cuiaba, Figueirense, Flamengo, Fluminense, Fortaleza, Goias, Gremio, Internacional, Joinville, Juventude, Nautico, Palmeiras, Parana, Ponte Preta, Portuguesa, Red Bull Bragantino, Santa Cruz, Santos, Sao Paulo, Sport, Vasco da Gama, Vitoria.\n\nCross-file additions: Athletico Paranaense (BR-Football/Cup), Atletico Goianiense (BR-Football = Atletico-GO), Atletico Mineiro (BR-Football/Cup), Botafogo PB, Botafogo SP, Bragantino (BR-Football = RB Bragantino SP!), Bragantino PA (different, Pará), America RN, America MG, EC Bahia, EC Juventude, EC Vitoria, Fortaleza EC/FC, Nautico Capibaribe, Operario PR, Sport Recife, Sao Paulo, Vasco Da Gama RJ, Vila Nova, Portuguesa Desportos, Guarani SP, CSA... \n\nLibertadores Brazilian teams: Flamengo, Fluminense, Palmeiras, Corinthians, Sao Paulo, Santos, Gremio, Atletico-MG, Atletico-PR/Athletico, Cruzeiro, Internacional, Botafogo, Chapecoense, Fortaleza, America-MG, Red Bull Bragantino, Vasco, Avai? (Avai not in Lib list... fine).\n\nForeign Libertadores teams: Boca Juniors, River Plate, etc. — these don't need Brazilian club registry entries; they resolve via fallback normalized identity. But careful with alias collisions like \"Nacional (URU)\" vs \"Nacional (PAR)\" vs \"Nacional - AM\" (Brazilian Amazonas club) vs \"Nacional-URU\". Fallback normalization must KEEP the parenthetical for foreign teams to distinguish! My normalize function drops parentheticals... For Libertadores, \"(URU)\", \"(PAR)\", \"-EQU\", \"-PAR\" suffixes distinguish same-named foreign clubs. If I drop them, \"Nacional (URU)\" and \"Nacional (PAR)\" and \"Nacional-AM\" all collapse to \"nacional\". That breaks head-to-head for Nacional vs Nacional.\n\nRefined normalization strategy for matching raw names → club identity:\n\n```python\ndef normalize_team_name(raw):\n    # 1. Deaccent, lowercase\n    # 2. Remove trailing \" - XX\" / \"-XX\" state qualifier ONLY if XX is a Brazilian UF code (27 known codes)\n    #    and NOT if it's a foreign country code (URU, PAR, EQU, ARG, CHI, COL, BOL, PER, MEX, VEN, USA)?\n    #    e.g. \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Olimpia-PAR\", \"Guaraní (PAR)\".\n    # 3. Keep parentheticals? For Brazilian club registry matching, parenthetical content like\n    #    \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\" should be dropped; for foreign, \"(URU)\" must be kept as country.\n```\n\nDesign decision: the canonical club registry contains explicit aliases for every Brazilian club variant, INCLUDING state forms (\"flamengo rj\") and full-name forms. For raw names not in the registry (foreign teams, tiny clubs), the fallback identity = normalize WITHOUT dropping anything meaningful:\n- deaccent, lowercase\n- drop parentheticals that are NOT country qualifiers? No wait — \"Nacional (URU)\" vs \"Nacional (PAR)\": keep the parenthetical. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\": registry alias \"boavista sport club antigo esporte clube barreira rj\"? Ugly. Simpler: fallback normalization converts \" (URU)\" → \"-uru\" style suffix... \n\nCleanest fallback: deaccent, lowercase, strip punctuation to spaces but KEEP parenthetical content as words: \"nacional uru\", \"nacional par\", \"guarani par\", \"boavista sport club antigo esporte clube barreira rj\". Then also produce a \"short\" form dropping parentheticals entirely (\"nacional\", \"guarani\") for display. Identity = full form; display = prettified.\n\nFor Brazilian clubs, the registry wins before fallback (since aliases cover the state-suffixed and parenthetical forms). E.g. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" — do I have it in the registry? It's a one-off tiny club (2 matches). Fallback: normalized \"boavista sport club antigo esporte clube barreira rj\"... but wait — dropping parenthetical gives \"boavista sport club rj\" while another entry is \"Boavista - RJ\" → \"boavista rj\". These wouldn't match each other! For tiny clubs with messy names, imperfect matching is acceptable — they're not in the spec's queries. But wait: Brasileirao/Cup \"Boavista - RJ\" vs BR-Football \"Boavista RJ\" → \"boavista rj\" both — they match. The \"(antigo...)\" one doesn't. Fine — acceptable, tiny club.\n\nSo the algorithm:\n\n```python\ndef team_key(raw):\n    \"\"\"Canonical lookup key for a raw team string.\"\"\"\n    s = deaccent(raw).lower()\n    s = re.sub(r'\\([^)]*\\)', r' \\1 ', s)?  # keep paren content: \"(URU)\" -> \" uru \"\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, let me define precisely:\n\n```python\ndef _base_key(raw: str) -> str:\n    s = strip_accents(raw).lower()\n    s = s.replace('(', ' ').replace(')', ' ')\n    s = re.sub(r'[.\\-]', ' ', s)   # punctuation to space... \n```\n\nWait \"A.s.a. - AL\" → \"a s a al\". And \"Asa - AL\" → \"asa al\". \"ASA\" BR-Football → \"asa\". Ugh, \"A.s.a.\" vs \"Asa\". Special-case: remove dots WITHOUT adding space when they're intra-word: \"a.s.a.\" → \"asa\". So: first remove dots (no space), then other punctuation → space.\n\nState suffix stripping for the *base* (without state) key: remove trailing Brazilian UF two-letter token. UF list: AC, AL, AM, AP, BA, CE, DF, ES, GO, MA, MG, MS, MT, PA, PB, PE, PI, PR, RJ, RN, RO, RR, RS, SC, SE, SP, TO. Foreign 3-letter codes (URU, PAR, EQU, ARG...) are NOT stripped by this rule (they're 3 letters). \n\nSo \"Atletico-MG\" → key \"atletico mg\", base \"atletico mg\" (MG kept in key; base-without-state \"atletico\"). \"Nacional (URU)\" → key \"nacional uru\", base \"nacional uru\" (URU is not a UF so it stays; base-without-state stays \"nacional uru\"). Hmm — but then \"Nacional-URU\" → \"nacional uru\" matches \"Nacional (URU)\" → \"nacional uru\". And \"Guaraní (PAR)\" → \"guarani par\" matches \"Guaraní-PAR\" → \"guarani par\". \n\nRegistry alias matching: each curated club lists aliases as *keys* (with state) AND claims the *base* (without state) IF unambiguous. Query resolution:\n1. key(query) ∈ alias_index → club\n2. base(query) ∈ base_index (club whose base alias matches) → club if unique\n3. prefix/substring search → candidates list\n\nExample: raw \"Atletico-PR\" → key \"atletico pr\" ∈ aliases of club atletico_pr ✓. Raw \"Athletico Paranaense\" (BR-Football) → key \"athletico paranaense\" ∈ aliases of atletico_pr ✓ (curated). Raw \"Athletico\" (Libertadores) → key \"athletico\" — curated alias of atletico_pr ✓. Raw \"Atlético - PR\" (Cup) → \"atletico pr\" ✓. Raw \"Atletico Paranaense\" → \"atletico paranaense\" ✓.\n\nRaw \"Atletico-MG\" → \"atletico mg\" ∈ atletico_mg aliases ✓. \"Atlético Mineiro\" → \"atletico mineiro\" ∈ atletico_mg aliases ✓ (curated).\n\nRaw \"América-MG\" (Cup/novo) → \"america mg\" ∈ america_mg aliases ✓. BR-Football \"America MG\" → \"america mg\" ✓. FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"america fc minas gerais\" ∈ america_mg aliases ✓ (curated).\n\nQuery \"Flamengo\" → key \"flamengo\" ∈ flamengo aliases ✓ → Flamengo (RJ). Query \"Flamengo-PI\" → \"flamengo pi\" ∈ flamengo_pi aliases. \n\nFor matching to also work between \"Sport-PE\" (Brasileirao) and \"Sport Recife\" (BR-Football) and \"Sport Club do Recife\" (FIFA): club sport_recife aliases {\"sport pe\"? no wait: key of \"Sport-PE\" is \"sport pe\"...}. Hmm wait: \"Sport-PE\" → key \"sport pe\". So aliases for sport_recife: {\"sport\", \"sport pe\", \"sport recife\", \"sport club recife\", \"sport club do recife\"}. Base claim \"sport\". But BR-Football has \"Sport Boys\" (Peruvian!) → key \"sport boys\" — not matching base \"sport\" exactly, fine.\n\nNow \"Corinthians-SP\" → \"corinthians sp\" ∈ corinthians aliases {\"corinthians\", \"corinthians sp\"}. \n\n\"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → \"vasco da gama rj\"; \"Vasco da Gama - RJ\" → \"vasco da gama rj\"; \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → \"vasco da gama rj\"; \"Vasco\" → \"vasco\". Club vasco aliases: {\"vasco\", \"vasco rj\"? does \"Vasco-RJ\" appear? no, \"vasco\" bare in novo/Libertadores, \"vasco da gama rj\" elsewhere}. Include both.\n\n\"Botafogo-RJ\" → \"botafogo rj\"; \"Botafogo\" (Lib) → \"botafogo\"; BR-Football \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"botafogo rj\". Club botafogo_rj aliases {\"botafogo\", \"botafogo rj\", \"botafogo de futebol e regatas\"}. Botafogo-PB: {\"botafogo pb\"}; Botafogo-SP: {\"botafogo sp\"}.\n\n\"São Paulo-SP\" → \"sao paulo sp\"; \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → \"sao paulo sp\"; \"Sao Paulo\" → \"sao paulo\". ✓\n\n\"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → \"red bull bragantino sp\"; \"Bragantino - SP\" (Cup) → \"bragantino sp\"; BR-Football \"Bragantino\" → \"bragantino\"; Lib \"Red Bull Bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\". All → club rb_bragantino aliases {\"bragantino\", \"red bull bragantino\", \"red bull bragantino sp\", \"rb bragantino\"}. Bragantino-PA separate: {\"bragantino pa\"}.\n\n\"Fortaleza-CE\" → \"fortaleza ce\"; \"Fortaleza\" (Lib) → \"fortaleza\"; \"Fortaleza EC\"/\"Fortaleza FC\" (BR-Football) → \"fortaleza ec\"/\"fortaleza fc\". Club fortaleza aliases {\"fortaleza\", \"fortaleza ce\", \"fortaleza ec\", \"fortaleza fc\"}.\n\n\"Internacional-RS\" → \"internacional rs\"; \"Internacional\" → \"internacional\"; \"Internacional - RS\" → \"internacional rs\"; \"EC Internacional SC\"? That's Internacional de Lages (SC) — different club, alias \"internacional sc\"... hmm \"EC Internacional SC\" → key \"ec internacional sc\". Distinct from \"internacional rs\". OK — curated aliases only on the main Inter: {\"internacional\", \"internacional rs\"}. The SC one falls to fallback: key \"ec internacional sc\". Fine.\n\n\"Goiás-GO\" → \"goias go\"; \"Goiás - GO\" → \"goias go\"; \"Goias\" → \"goias\". ✓\n\n\"Ceará-CE\" → \"ceara ce\"; \"Ceara\" → \"ceara\"; \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → \"ceara sporting club\". ✓\n\n\"Chapecoense-SC\" → \"chapecoense sc\"; \"Chapecoense\" → \"chapecoense\". ✓\n\n\"Paraná-PR\" → \"parana pr\"; \"Paraná\" → \"parana\"; \"Paraná Clube\"... key \"ca parana\" (BR-Football \"CA Parana\")! and \"CA Parana\" → \"ca parana\" — curated alias of parana_clube {\"ca parana\", \"parana clube\", \"parana\"?}. Careful: bare \"parana\" claimed by Paraná Clube (the main Parana). ✓\n\n\"Juventude-RS\" → \"juventude rs\"; \"Juventude\" → \"juventude\"; \"EC Juventude\" → \"ec juventude\". ✓\n\n\"Náutico-PE\" → \"nautico pe\"; \"Náutico\" → \"nautico\"; \"Nautico Capibaribe\" → \"nautico capibaribe\". ✓\n\n\"Portuguesa-SP\" → \"portuguesa sp\"; \"Portuguesa Desportos\" → \"portuguesa desportos\". ✓\n\n\"Ponte Preta-SP\" → \"ponte preta sp\"; \"Ponte Preta\" → \"ponte preta\". ✓\n\n\"Santa Cruz-PE\" → \"santa cruz pe\"; \"Santa Cruz\" → \"santa cruz\"; \"Santa Cruz FC\" → \"santa cruz fc\". ✓\n\n\"CSA-AL\" → \"csa al\" (\"Csa-AL\" → \"csa al\"); \"CSA\" → \"csa\". ✓\n\n\"Criciúma-SC\" → \"criciuma sc\"; \"Criciuma\" → \"criciuma\". ✓\n\n\"Coritiba-PR\" → \"coritiba pr\"; \"Coritiba\" → \"coritiba\". ✓\n\n\"Figueirense-SC\" → \"figueirense sc\"; \"Figueirense\" → \"figueirense\". ✓\n\n\"Cuiaba-MT\" → \"cuiaba mt\"; \"Cuiabá - MT\" → \"cuiaba mt\"; \"Cuiaba\" → \"cuiaba\". ✓\n\n\"Avai-SC\" → \"avai sc\"; \"Avaí\" → \"avai\"; \"Avaí - SC\" → \"avai sc\". ✓\n\n\"Vitoria-BA\" → \"vitoria ba\"; \"Vitória - BA\" → \"vitoria ba\"; \"Vitória\" → \"vitoria\"; \"EC Vitoria\" → \"ec vitoria\". Careful: Vitória-ES (\"Vitoria F. C. - ES\" → \"vitoria f c es\", \"Vitoria ES\" → \"vitoria es\") separate club. ✓ (base \"vitoria\" claimed by Vitória-BA as the major club; ES variants have their own keys.)\n\n\"Bahia-BA\" → \"bahia ba\"; \"Bahia\" → \"bahia\"; \"EC Bahia\" → \"ec bahia\". ✓\n\n\"Cruzeiro-MG\" → \"cruzeiro mg\"; \"Cruzeiro\" → \"cruzeiro\". ✓\n\n\"Grêmio-RS\" → \"gremio rs\"; \"Grêmio\" → \"gremio\". ✓ (Grêmio Novorizontino etc. have own keys, don't claim \"gremio\".)\n\n\"America-MG\"/\"América - MG\" → \"america mg\"; \"América-RN\"/\"América - RN\" → \"america rn\"; \"América de Natal - RN\" → \"america de natal rn\" (alias of america_rn); \"America FC Natal\" → \"america fc natal\" (alias of america_rn); \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"america fc minas gerais\" (alias of america_mg). ✓\n\n\"Atletico-GO\"/\"Atlético - GO\" → \"atletico go\"; \"Atletico Goianiense\" → \"atletico goianiense\" (alias of atletico_go). ✓\n\n\"Guarani\" (novo) → \"guarani\"; \"Guarani - SP\" → \"guarani sp\"; \"Guarani SP\" → \"guarani sp\". ✓ base \"guarani\" → guarani_sp.\n\n\"Atletico Acreano\" → own club (fallback). \"Atlético Cearense\" → fallback. Etc.\n\nFor foreign Libertadores clubs, fallback identity: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → \"barcelona equ\"; \"Barcelona-EQU\"... also FIFA \"FC Barcelona\" → \"fc barcelona\" — distinct, good.\n\nNow, FIFA club matching for players_by_club: FIFA clubs are mostly foreign (\"Juventus\", \"Liverpool\") plus 15 Brazilian ones. Query \"Flamengo players\" → club resolution → flamengo → FIFA lookup for aliases of flamengo → none → return empty with note. Query \"Grêmio\" → aliases {\"gremio\", \"gremio rs\"} → FIFA club \"Grêmio\" normalizes to \"gremio\" → match → 20 players. \n\nFor the \"players_at_brazilian_clubs\" summary, I need to know which FIFA clubs are Brazilian: registry-driven — for each curated club, include optional `fifa_names: [\"Grêmio\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", ...]` mapping to the exact FIFA Club strings. \n\nOK — curation plan settled. Also the DERBY registry:\n\nKnown Brazilian derbies (pairs of canonical ids):\n- Fla-Flu: Flamengo x Fluminense\n- Clássico dos Milhões: Vasco x Flamengo\n- Clássico Vovô: Fluminense x Vasco... actually \"Clássico Vovô\" = Fluminense vs Vasco? Hmm, it's Botafogo vs Fluminense? Let me be careful: \"Clássico Vovô\" (the Grandfather derby) is Fluminense vs Vasco da Gama — oldest derby in Rio? Actually Botafogo x Fluminense is the oldest derby in Brazil (\"Clássico Vovô\"). Yes — Botafogo–Fluminense, played since 1905, is called Clássico Vovô.\n- Grenal: Grêmio x Internacional\n- Clássico Majestoso: Corinthians x São Paulo\n- Derby Paulista: Corinthians x Palmeiras\n- Choque-Rei: São Paulo x Palmeiras\n- Clássico Alvinegro? (Santos x São Paulo?) — \"Clássico da Vila\"? Santos derbies: Santos x Corinthians? I'll include the famous ones:\n  - Ba-Vi: Bahia x Vitória\n- Clássico-Rei: Cruzeiro x Atlético-MG\n- Clássico dos Gigantes: Fluminense x Vasco? no... let me just use well-documented ones:\n  - Fla-Flu (Flamengo × Fluminense)\n  - Clássico dos Milhões (Flamengo × Vasco)\n  - Clássico Vovô (Botafogo × Fluminense)\n  - Clássico da Rivalidade (Fluminense × Vasco)? skip\n  - Grenal (Grêmio × Internacional)\n  - Clássico Majestoso (Corinthians × São Paulo)\n  - Derby Paulista / O Derby (Corinthians × Palmeiras)\n  - Choque-Rei (São Paulo × Palmeiras)\n  - San-São (Santos × São Paulo)\n  - Clássico da Saudade? (Palmeiras × Santos — \"Clássico da Saudade\") yes that's Palmeiras × Santos.\n  - Ba-Vi (Bahia × Vitória)\n  - Clássico-Rei (Cruzeiro × Atlético Mineiro)\n  - Clássico das Emoções? Ceará x Fortaleza = \"Clássico-Rei do Norte\"? The Ceará x Fortaleza derby is \"Clássico-Rei\". Hmm, multiple \"Clássico-Rei\". I'll label Ceará x Fortaleza as \"Clássico-Rei (Ceará x Fortaleza)\". \n  - Come-Facil? skip. \n  - Atletiba: Atlético-PR × Coritiba ✓\n  - Didi-Facil? no. \n  - Clássico dos Ipês? skip. Keep it to ~12 solid ones:\n  - also \"Clássico Vésti\"? no.\n\nGood set: Fla-Flu, Milhões, Vovô, Grenal, Majestoso, Derby Paulista, Choque-Rei, San-São, Saudade, Ba-Vi, Clássico-Rei (MG), Atletiba, Ceará-Fortaleza (Clássico-Rei cearense).\n\n**Competitions normalization**: The competition universe:\n- \"Brasileirão Série A\" — sources: Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2021), novo (2003-2019), BR-Football \"Serie A\" (2014-2023).\n- \"Copa do Brasil\" — Brazilian_Cup_Matches (2012-2021), BR-Football \"Copa do Brasil\" (2023? range 2014-2023).\n- \"Copa Libertadores\" — Libertadores_Matches (2013-2022).\n- \"Série B\", \"Série C\" — BR-Football only.\n\nFor standings:\n- Serie A: season 2003-2011 → novo; 2012-2019 → either novo or Brasileirao file (both have it — dedupe or pick one); 2012-2021 → Brasileirao; 2022-2023 → BR-Football. Strategy: choose single source per (competition, season) by priority, never mixing. Priority for Serie A: Brasileirao_Matches > novo > BR-Football. So 2012-2019 uses Brasileirao file, 2003-2011 novo, 2022-2023 BR-Football. But BR-Football \"Serie A\" 2014-2023 overlaps too; using it only for 2022-2023. Wait — does BR-Football Serie A have 2022, 2023? Range 2014-05-21 to 2023-12-07 across all tournaments. Serie A 2022/2023 in BR-Football: yes probably. Let me verify later in tests (I'll test 2023 standings: who won 2023 Brasileirão? Palmeiras. In BR-Football data check).\n\nHmm wait, actually there's a subtlety: BR-Football Serie A team names are unambiguous-ish and the file includes 2022 and 2023. Let me verify quickly that BR-Football has full Serie A 2022/2023 seasons.\n\n- Copa do Brasil: Cup_Matches (2012-2021) > BR-Football (2022-2023?). Cup finals: round 8 (two legs).\n\nAlso for the \"winner\" of a competition: standings[0]. For Copa do Brasil winner: the final (round 8) two-legged aggregate — computing the cup winner needs aggregate logic (which team advances/wins over two legs). That's doable: group finals by season, aggregate goals over two legs, apply away-goals rule? Historically Copa do Brasil used away goals until 2021... and penalties not in data. If aggregate tie → \"decided on penalties (not in data)\". I'll implement aggregate winner with a note when tied. Nice-to-have for \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\".\n\nFor Libertadores finals: stage == \"final\", two legs, aggregate → winner.\n\n**Answer formatting**: The spec shows formatted text answers. My tools return structured data (dicts/lists) — MCP best practice — but also include a `summary` formatted string in the style of the spec examples. I'll return JSON-serializable dicts with both `summary` (human-formatted text block) and structured fields.\n\n**MCP tools** (each maps to spec query categories):\n1. `search_matches(team, opponent, competition, season, date_from, date_to, stage, limit)` — match queries\n2. `head_to_head(team_a, team_b)` — head-to-head\n3. `team_stats(team, season, competition,