{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788239528088,"sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-825e2306e3174e5e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint(\"Brasileirao per season:\", dict(sorted(collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in rows).items())))\n# 2019 champion check\npts=collections.defaultdict(lambda: [0]*6)\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['season']!='2019': continue\n    hg,ag=int(r['home_goal']),int(r['away_goal'])\n    for t,gf,ga in ((r['home_team'],hg,ag),(r['away_team'],ag,hg)):\n        rec=pts[t]; rec[3]+=gf; rec[4]+=ga\n        if gf>ga: rec[0]+=1; rec[5]+=3\n        elif gf==ga: rec[1]+=1; rec[5]+=1\n        else: rec[2]+=1\nfor t,(w,d,l,gf,ga,s) in sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1][5])[:4]:\n    print(f\"  {t}: {s} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L, {gf}:{ga})\")\nprint(\"n teams 2019:\", len(pts))\n# Cup finals by season: round 8\nwith open(p+'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    cup=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nfin = collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in cup if r['round']=='8')\nprint(\"Cup round-8 per season:\", dict(sorted(fin.items())))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-8c2c162e81b7"},"output":"Brasileirao per season: {'2012': 380, '2013': 380, '2014': 380, '2015': 380, '2016': 380, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 380, '2021': 380, '2022': 380}\n  Flamengo-RJ: 90 pts (28W 6D 4L, 86:37)\n  Santos-SP: 74 pts (22W 8D 8L, 60:33)\n  Palmeiras-SP: 74 pts (21W 11D 6L, 61:32)\n  Gremio-RS: 65 pts (19W 8D 11L, 64:39)\nn teams 2019: 20\nCup round-8 per season: {'2013': 2, '2014': 2, '2015': 2, '2017': 2, '2018': 2, '2019': 2, '2020': 2}\n","metadata":{"output":"Brasileirao per season: {'2012': 380, '2013': 380, '2014': 380, '2015': 380, '2016': 380, '2017': 380, '2018': 380, '2019': 380, '2020': 380, '2021': 380, '2022': 380}\n  Flamengo-RJ: 90 pts (28W 6D 4L, 86:37)\n  Santos-SP: 74 pts (22W 8D 8L, 60:33)\n  Palmeiras-SP: 74 pts (21W 11D 6L, 61:32)\n  Gremio-RS: 65 pts (19W 8D 11L, 64:39)\nn teams 2019: 20\nCup round-8 per season: {'2013': 2, '2014': 2, '2015': 2, '2017': 2, '2018': 2, '2019': 2, '2020': 2}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint(\"Brasileirao per season:\", dict(sorted(collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in rows).items())))\n# 2019 champion check\npts=collections.defaultdict(lambda: [0]*6)\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['season']!='2019': continue\n    hg,ag=int(r['home_goal']),int(r['away_goal'])\n    for t,gf,ga in ((r['home_team'],hg,ag),(r['away_team'],ag,hg)):\n        rec=pts[t]; rec[3]+=gf; rec[4]+=ga\n        if gf>ga: rec[0]+=1; rec[5]+=3\n        elif gf==ga: rec[1]+=1; rec[5]+=1\n        else: rec[2]+=1\nfor t,(w,d,l,gf,ga,s) in sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv:-kv[1][5])[:4]:\n    print(f\"  {t}: {s} pts ({w}W {d}D {l}L, {gf}:{ga})\")\nprint(\"n teams 2019:\", len(pts))\n# Cup finals by season: round 8\nwith open(p+'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    cup=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nfin = collections.Counter(r['season'] for r in cup if r['round']=='8')\nprint(\"Cup round-8 per season:\", dict(sorted(fin.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788239528084,"end":1788239528087}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Hmm — 2023 Serie A from BRF gives Gremio 68 pts as top? But reality: Palmeiras won 2023 Brasileirão with 70 pts... and Botafogo led most of the season. 377 matches vs 380 expected — the BRF 2023 data is incomplete (3 matches missing) and gives a slightly wrong table (in reality: Palmeiras 70, Grêmio 68, Botafogo 64, Flamengo 64, Atlético-MG 63... wait actually real 2023 final: Palmeiras 70, Grêmio 68, Botafogo 64, Flamengo 64, Atlético-MG 63, São Paulo 63...). Hmm, BRF says Flamengo 66, GAM 66, Botafogo 64 — doesn't match reality exactly, meaning BRF data for 2023 is partially incomplete/corrupted. \n\nHmm wait, also 2021 BRF Serie A = 491 matches?? Serie A should have 380. 491 is too many — maybe includes duplicated matches or playoff/extra matches? 2021 Serie A had 38 rounds × 10 = 380. 491 is wrong... or includes some other rows. 2020: 264 — pandemic season, real count 351? Hmm, incomplete.\n\nSo BRF is partially unreliable. My standings tool computes FROM the data (spec says \"calculated from match results\") — the spec explicitly wants calculated standings, with the caveat they reflect the data provided. For 2023, my tool would report Grêmio on 68 (based on 377 matches). That's \"correct per data\" but factually wrong vs reality. The spec's success criterion is about the tool's capability, and it says standings are \"calculated from match results\". I'll compute from data and ALSO report the match count + a note when season data is incomplete (< expected 380 for Serie A with 20 teams; 240 for years with 12 teams in 2003-2005 era, etc.). I'll include `matches_counted` and a `data_completeness` note. For tests I'll assert against values computed from the data itself (self-consistent), not against real-world facts — except for cases where the data is known-good (e.g. 2019 Brasileirao from Brasileirao_Matches: Flamengo champion 90 pts — that matches reality AND the spec example: \"1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\" — the spec example literally gives the 2019 numbers! Let me verify the data gives exactly that: Flamengo 90 pts 28W 6D 4L. Great test case.)\n\nLet me verify 2019 from Brasileirao_Matches and 2018, and check the novo 2003 era team counts (20 teams 2003-2005 = 462 matches? Actually 2003 had 24 teams (462? no: 24 teams double round-robin = 552... hmm 2003 Brasileirão had 24 teams; 2004-2005 22 teams; 2006+ 20 teams). I'll compute per-season match counts and expected table sizes dynamically: teams count = distinct teams in season; expected matches = n*(n-1) if even... For a double round robin: n*(n-1) matches. I'll use that as the completeness check.\n\nAlso 2021 BRF Serie A 491 — with 20 teams, expected 380. So BRF has junk rows in 2021 (maybe duplicated with slightly different values). Standings selection priority: Brasileirao_Matches covers 2012-2021 (full). novo covers 2003-2019. So Serie A standings source: 2012-2021 → Brasileirao_Matches (perfect), 2003-2011 → novo, 2022-2023 → BRF (only option; flag incompleteness note).\n\nWait — but does Brasileirao_Matches have complete 2020? 2020 had 380 matches (20 teams). Earlier count: 4180 total over 2012-2021. 10 seasons × 380 = 3800 ≠ 4180. So some seasons have more teams: 2012-2015? No — 2012-2020 all had 20 teams... 2021 had 20. Hmm 4180/10 = 418 avg. Actually 2012-2019: 20 teams = 380/season; 2020: 20 teams; 2021: 20 teams... that's 3800. Unless earlier seasons had 24 teams (2012? no, 2012 had 20). Let me check per-season counts of Brasileirao_Matches. 4180 - 3800 = 380 extra — one season with 22 teams? Let me check.\n\nAlso, the Cup finals: round 8 = final (2 legs). Verify 2012-2021 all have round 8 = 2 matches.\n\nLet me run these checks.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b61b6e10011P0JVyBJV43QMM","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b616aae001BtWlm6tfX3hk7p"}}
