Let me fix: halftime home goals can't be directly derived... Actually ht_diff = home goals minus away goals at halftime. So halftime_home_goals isn't recoverable exactly, but (ht_diff, at_diff) — note at_diff seems to be... for the sample: 'ht_diff': '0.0', 'at_diff': '0.0', both DRAW. Second row: 'ht_diff': '-1.0', 'at_diff': '1.0' → Flamengo 0-1 São Paulo at half → ht_diff=-1 (home minus away), at_diff=+1 (away minus home). So at_diff = -ht_diff. I'll store halftime diff instead of halftime goals: stats.home_halftime_diff. Simpler: keep `halftime_diff` = ht_diff (home-away at half). Let me redefine MatchStats: halftime_home=None/away=None → replace with `halftime_diff: Optional[int]`. And add home/away result strings? Not needed.\n\nActually let me reconsider MatchStats fields:\n- home_corners, away_corners, home_shots, away_shots, home_attacks, away_attacks, total_corners, halftime_diff.\n\nUpdate models.py MatchStats accordingly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b66c16d001OXVryk63nsNgxQ","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b66b001001sToQBj0rmVkThH"}}
