{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788240048535,"sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd55ba5f1f1104c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\nfrom soccer_mcp.clubs import resolve_club\nfrom soccer_mcp.normalize import parse_datetime\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    brf=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f)]\nwith open(p+'Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    bra=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r['season']>='2014']\n\n# index brasileirao by (season, home_id, away_id) -> list of dates\nbidx = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in bra:\n    bidx[(r['season'], resolve_club(r['home_team']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away_team']).club_id)].append(parse_datetime(r['datetime'])[0])\n\ndiffs = collections.Counter(); nomatch=0; total=0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']!='Serie A': continue\n    d = parse_datetime(r['date'])[0]\n    season = str(d.year)\n    k = (season, resolve_club(r['home']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away']).club_id)\n    total += 1\n    if k not in bidx: nomatch+=1; continue\n    best = min(abs((d-x).days) for x in bidx[k])\n    diffs[best]+=1\nprint(\"Serie A rows:\", total, \"no fixture match (pairing not in file):\", nomatch)\nprint(\"date diff distribution:\", dict(sorted(diffs.items())))\n# same for Copa do Brasil\nwith open(p+'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    cup=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f)]\ncidx = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in cup:\n    cidx[(r['season'], resolve_club(r['home_team']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away_team']).club_id)].append(parse_datetime(r['datetime'])[0])\ncd = collections.Counter(); cn=0; ct=0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']!='Copa do Brasil': continue\n    d = parse_datetime(r['date'])[0]; season=str(d.year)\n    k = (season, resolve_club(r['home']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away']).club_id)\n    ct+=1\n    if k not in cidx: cn+=1; continue\n    cd[min(abs((d-x).days) for x in cidx[k])]+=1\nprint(\"Cup rows:\", ct, \"no fixture match:\", cn, dict(sorted(cd.items())))\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-8c2c162e81b7"},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 20, in <module>\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'club_id'\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 20, in <module>\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'club_id'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\nfrom soccer_mcp.clubs import resolve_club\nfrom soccer_mcp.normalize import parse_datetime\np='data/kaggle/'\nwith open(p+'BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    brf=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f)]\nwith open(p+'Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    bra=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r['season']>='2014']\n\n# index brasileirao by (season, home_id, away_id) -> list of dates\nbidx = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in bra:\n    bidx[(r['season'], resolve_club(r['home_team']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away_team']).club_id)].append(parse_datetime(r['datetime'])[0])\n\ndiffs = collections.Counter(); nomatch=0; total=0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']!='Serie A': continue\n    d = parse_datetime(r['date'])[0]\n    season = str(d.year)\n    k = (season, resolve_club(r['home']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away']).club_id)\n    total += 1\n    if k not in bidx: nomatch+=1; continue\n    best = min(abs((d-x).days) for x in bidx[k])\n    diffs[best]+=1\nprint(\"Serie A rows:\", total, \"no fixture match (pairing not in file):\", nomatch)\nprint(\"date diff distribution:\", dict(sorted(diffs.items())))\n# same for Copa do Brasil\nwith open(p+'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    cup=[r for r in csv.DictReader(f)]\ncidx = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in cup:\n    cidx[(r['season'], resolve_club(r['home_team']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away_team']).club_id)].append(parse_datetime(r['datetime'])[0])\ncd = collections.Counter(); cn=0; ct=0\nfor r in brf:\n    if r['tournament']!='Copa do Brasil': continue\n    d = parse_datetime(r['date'])[0]; season=str(d.year)\n    k = (season, resolve_club(r['home']).club_id, resolve_club(r['away']).club_id)\n    ct+=1\n    if k not in cidx: cn+=1; continue\n    cd[min(abs((d-x).days) for x in cidx[k])]+=1\nprint(\"Cup rows:\", ct, \"no fixture match:\", cn, dict(sorted(cd.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788240048530,"end":1788240048534}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting! America-MG 2-0 São Paulo was on 2021-12-**09** in the Brasileirao file but 2021-12-**10** in BRF. The fixture exists in both files with a ONE-DAY date difference. So BRF dates are often shifted by a day (probably timezone/conversion issue in the source dataset). That's why 240 rows didn't match on (date, teams).\n\nThis means my dedup key (family, date, home, away) fails to merge many BRF rows with Brasileirao rows — leaving near-duplicates that differ by date and double-count in match searches, team stats, H2H.\n\nOptions:\n1. Dedup key without date: (family, season, home, away, round?) — but cup two-legged ties have same teams twice per season! Serie A has each pairing twice per season (home/away reversed) — key (family, season, frozenset(teams)) would wrongly merge the two legs... unless I include the \"leg\" orientation: (family, season, home, away). Serie A: pairing appears twice (A home once, B home once) → keys distinct ✓. Cup: two legs are REVERSED home/away typically? Copa do Brasil two legs: first leg at team A, second at team B (reversed) → keys distinct ✓. But same-venue two legs? E.g. Libertadores finals sometimes both legs... no, always reversed. But Copa do Brasil round 1 (single match) vs round 2 (single match) — different opponents, no clash. What about a cup pairing meeting TWICE at the SAME venue in one season? Possible in Libertadores (group stage + knockout, or 2020-format)... e.g. two group matches are home/away reversed ✓. Knockout later vs same team — again reversed... could be same venue twice (e.g. finals played at one stadium? no). Edge case: rare. Risk of over-merging exists but is much smaller than the current under-merging problem.\n\nBut wait — there's a REAL case: Serie A 2020 had teams playing each other... no, always double round-robin. Serie B same. Serie C: format has groups; teams meet 4x? Serie C (BRF only) — third division has 2 groups of 10, teams in same group play each other 4 times (2 home + 2 away)! So key (family, season, home, away) would merge legit distinct Serie C matches (same pairing, same venue, twice per season). Hmm.\n\nSafer dedup key: (family, season, home, away, date±1 tolerance)? Date proximity matching is complex.\n\nAlternative approach: **make dedup date-exact (current) and accept the date-shifted stragglers, BUT filter BRF league rows for seasons covered by preferred files at the LOADER level.** I.e., data-tier selection: for each (family, season), choose ONE authoritative source before even building the match list... but then BR-Football's unique value (2022/2023 coverage, stats, Serie B/C) is lost for overlapping seasons — stats are only on BRF rows! E.g. \"show corners for Flamengo vs Fluminense 2019\" — only BRF has corners.\n\nHmm. Balance: The BRF row for a fixture that's ALSO in Brasileirao adds only stats (scores identical? presumably). The fixture set from Brasileirao is complete for 2012-2022 Serie A. The BRF-only fixtures for those seasons are either (a) date-shifted duplicates, or (b) junk rows (Vasco/Coritiba 2021 \"Serie A\" — 240 unmatched include Vasco? The unmatched counter showed gremio 16, sport 15... let me check if vasco rows are among the unmatched).\n\nWait — actually the unmatched 240 include both date-shifted duplicates AND the extra teams (Vasco, Coritiba, Goiás, Botafogo ~10-12 rows each = ~45 rows). The date-shifted ones (~195?) are duplicates of real fixtures.\n\nLet me think about what maximizes correctness for the spec's queries:\n\n**Standings**: use single authoritative source per (family, season) — preferred file if available (Brasileirao 2012-2022, novo 2003-2011, cup file 2012-2021, lib file, BRF only as fallback: serie_a 2023, serie_b/c always). This is solid.\n\n**Match searches / H2H / team stats / derbies**: polluted by BRF stragglers for overlapping seasons. Options:\n- A) Date±1 dedup: merge BRF row into Brasileirao row when same (family, season, home, away) and |date diff| ≤ 1. This kills both date-shifted dups AND same-day dups, while keeping Serie C 4-meetings intact? No — Serie C same-venue meetings would be same (family, season, home, away) with different dates > 1 apart? They're weeks apart, so ±1 tolerance won't merge them ✓. Cup legs: reversed venues, same pairing within a round pair — first leg A-home, second leg B-home → different keys ✓. But a cup pairing playing twice with SAME orientation within 3 days? Doesn't happen.\n  So dedup v2: group by (family, season, home, away, date_bucket) where date_bucket = the date of... hmm, need a proper algorithm: sort rows of same (family, season, home, away) by date, and merge consecutive rows whose dates are within 1 day AND from different sources (or same source? within-source dupes don't exist — BRF has no internal dups per my check... well 2021 BRF had 0 duplicate fixtures internally).\n  \n  Simpler greedy: for each (family, season, home, away) group sorted by date: walk rows; if the previous kept row's date is within 1 day of current row's date → merge into it (same fixture, keep primary = stats-rich/priority). Else new fixture. \n\n  Edge risk: a REAL pair of matches same pairing same venue 2 days apart — doesn't exist in these competitions.\n\n- B) Drop BRF rows for (family, season) combos covered by preferred files entirely; lose stats for those seasons. \n\nOption A is better — keeps stats, kills duplicates. But wait: what about BRF \"Serie A\" 2021 Vasco/Coritiba/Goiás/Botafogo rows — those fixtures don't exist in Brasileirao 2021 (those teams weren't in Serie A) so they survive as \"Serie A\" matches. They're actually Serie B matches mislabeled as Serie A in BRF! Do they also appear in BRF's \"Serie B\" 2021? BRF Serie B 2021 = 446 rows (expected 380). 446 - 380 = 66 ≈ the extra rows (491-380=111 Serie A extras + 66 Serie B extras — hmm 111 + 66 = 177 ≈ but some are date-shifted dups).\n\nLet me check: does BRF 2021 Serie B contain Vasco vs Botafogo fixtures? If both \"Serie A\" and \"Serie B\" have the same Vasco-Botafogo fixture, then after my (family, season, home, away) dedup they'd stay separate (different family). Mislabeling remains: Vasco \"Serie A\" 2021 rows.\n\nDetect mislabels: for a (family, season), if a team plays fewer than X% of matches in the preferred source... I can implement a **season-coverage cleanup**: for (family=serie_a, season) covered by Brasileirao file: teams appearing in the preferred file for that season define the valid team set; BRF rows involving teams NOT in that set for that season are discarded as mislabeled. Rows involving valid teams but not matching a preferred fixture (date-shifted) get merged via ±1 tolerance or... hmm, if the date shift is > 1 day they'd survive as extra fixtures.\n\nHow big is the >1day mismatch problem? The sample showed 12-10 vs 12-09 (1 day). Let me measure the date-diff distribution for BRF 2021 Serie A rows vs Brasileirao 2021 fixtures matched on (family, season, home, away) — pairing them by order? Messy. Quick test: for BRF rows whose teams are valid 2021 Serie A teams, check how many have an exact (date) match, how many have ±1 match, and how many have no match within ±1.\n\nLet me run that measurement, then finalize the dedup design. Also do the same for other overlap seasons (2014-2020) and Copa do Brasil (BRF cup vs Cup file).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b69a89c001nmVYnOO4128HMS","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b6954db001QkWy6CUnZlDToa"}}
