continue\n    cd[min(abs((d-x).days) for x in cidx[k])]+=1\nprint(\"Cup rows:\", ct, \"pairing not in cup file:\", cn, cnteams.most_common(4))\nprint(\"cup date diffs:\", dict(sorted(cd.items())))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788240053312,"end":1788240053321}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"A BRF team resolved to None via resolve_club? resolve_club returns None only if the alias isn't found — then fallback should apply. In my script I used resolve_club directly (not fallback). BRF team names that don't resolve: e.g. \"tuntum EC\"? normalize \"tuntum ec\" → not in registry → None. Right — in loaders I use resolver.resolve (fallback included). Let me fix the script to use fallback_club.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b69bbd2001xfuc0yZcm3TEy4","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b69b2bc001gAIF4gOr7zscqr"}}
