.csv\"),\n    COPA_DO_BRASIL: (\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\",),\n    LIBERTADORES: (\"Libertadores_Matches.csv\",),\n}\n\n@staticmethod\ndef _merge_fixture(primary, other):\n    extras = {primary.source} | set(primary.also_in_sources) | {other.source} | set(other.also_in_sources)\n    merged = primary\n    updates = {}\n    if merged.stage is None and other.stage: updates['stage']=other.stage; updates['round']=other.round\n    if merged.date is None and other.date: updates['date']=other.date\n    if merged.stadium is None and other.stadium: updates['stadium']=other.stadium\n    if merged.stats is None and other.stats: updates['stats']=other.stats\n    if updates: merged = replace(merged, **updates)\n    if extras != {primary.source} | set(primary.also_in_sources):\n        merged = replace(merged, also_in_sources=tuple(sorted(extras - {primary.source})))\n    return merged\n\n@classmethod\ndef _dedupe(cls, raw):\n    by_family_season = defaultdict(list)\n    for m in raw: by_family_season[(m.family, m.season)].append(m)\n    out = []\n    stats = {\"dropped_unmatched_rows\": 0}\n    for (family, season), rows in by_family_season.items():\n        preferred = PREFERRED_SOURCES.get(family, ())\n        present = [s for s in preferred if any(r.source==s for r in rows)]\n        if not present:\n            # no authoritative file covers this season: exact-date dedup only\n            seen = {}\n            for r in sorted(rows, key=cls._richness, reverse=True):\n                k=(r.date, r.home_team, r.away_team)\n                if k in seen: seen[k]=cls._merge_fixture(seen[k], r)\n                else: seen[k]=r\n            out.extend(seen.values())\n            continue\n        top = present[0]\n        base_lists = defaultdict(list)\n        others = []\n        for r in rows:\n            if r.source==top: base_lists[(r.home_team, r.away_team)].append(r)\n            else: others.append(r)\n        # if multiple base rows for same pairing (data anomaly) keep them all distinct\n        merged_map = {}\n        multi = []\n        for key, lst in base_lists.items():\n            if len(lst)==1: merged_map[key]=lst[0]\n            else: multi.extend(lst)\n        for r in others:\n            key=(r.home_team, r.away_team)\n            if key in merged_map: merged_map[key]=cls._merge_fixture(merged_map[key], r)\n            else: stats[\"dropped_unmatched_rows\"]+=1\n        out.extend(merged_map.values()); out.extend(multi)\n    out.sort(...)\n```\n\nWait — `_richness` for the no-preferred branch: rows sorted by (stats present, priority) — merge duplicates within BRF? There are no within-BRF (family, season, date, pairing) duplicates. But BRF cup 2022/2023: unique. OK keep that branch anyway as safety.\n\nHmm, also — the no-preferred branch happens for (family, season) groups where preferred files have no coverage: serie_b/c (BRF only), serie_a 2023, cup 2022/2023. ✓.\n\nBut WAIT: there's a subtle issue with `present[0]` — \"highest priority preferred source PRESENT\". For serie_a 2012-2019, both Brasileirao AND novo are present → top = Brasileirao (first in tuple) ✓; novo rows merged into Brasileirao pairings ✓; novo-only pairings (data gaps) → dropped ✓. For serie_a 2003-2011: only novo present → top = novo ✓. For serie_a 2022: Brasileirao ✓. Cup 2012-2021: cup file ✓. Lib: lib file ✓ (always).\n\n`dropped_unmatched_rows` — expose in a data-quality attribute; count expected: serie_a: BRF 2021 mislabels (~45?) + 2023 (no — 2023 has no preferred → not dropped, kept). Wait, serie_a 2023: preferred = Brasileirao (not present for 2023) → `present` empty → no-preferred branch → kept ✓.\n\nWhat gets dropped: BRF serie_a rows 2014-2022 with pairings not in Brasileirao (2021 mislabeled Serie B teams ~40 rows) + novo rows 2012-2019 not matching Brasileirao pairings (if any) + BRF cup rows 2014-2021 with pairings not in cup file (523 - 233(2022/23) = ~290 rows — WAIT that's a lot!).\n\nHmm, 290 BRF cup rows dropped for 2014-2021 sea