, [\"sao raimundo rr\"]),\n+    _club(\"moto_clube\", \"Moto Club\", \"MA\",\n+          [\"moto clube\", \"moto club\", \"moto club de sao luis\"]),\n ]\n \n CLUBS: dict[str, Club] = {c.club_id: c for c in _CLUBS}\n \n","additions":24,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/clubs.py","time":{"start":1788240181447,"end":1788240181449}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Excellent analysis. 88 collision bases, most of which are the SAME club with/without state (\"luverdense\"/\"luverdense mt\" — same club). The genuinely DIFFERENT clubs sharing a base:\n\n- `central`: central pe vs central sc — different clubs\n- `comercial`: comercial ms vs comercial pi — different\n- `operario`: operario ms vs operario mt — different (and \"Operario PR\" is curated)\n- `penarol`: \"penarol\" (no uf — Penarol of Montevideo? In Libertadores? no... \"Penarol AM\" and bare \"penarol\"? The bare one — from Libertadores \"Peñarol\" (URU)! ✓ foreign)\n- `river`: river ac vs river pi — different Brazilian clubs\n- `river plate`: \"river plate\" (ARG) vs \"river plate se\"?? River-SE (Sergipe) — different!\n- `rio branco`: rio branco ac vs rio branco es — different\n- `santa cruz`: santa cruz rn vs santa cruz rs — different (santa cruz PE is curated)\n- `sao francisco`: ac vs pa — different\n- `sao jose`: pa vs rs — different\n- `sao raimundo`: am, pa, rr — three different clubs\n\nSo my plan: fallback identity = base key (UF-stripped) — which unifies the same-club variants across files — PLUS curate the 11 genuinely-distinct same-base groups so their keys stay separate. For curated entries of these small clubs, I create clubs with aliases covering both state-suffixed and bare forms? NO — careful: if I curate \"central_pe\" with alias \"central pe\" and \"central_sc\" with \"central sc\", then bare \"central\" (if it appears anywhere) would be ambiguous → falls back to base \"central\" → creates a THIRD identity matching neither. Does bare \"Central\" appear? From the collision list, central has only PE and SC forms — no bare. Same for comercial, operario, river, rio branco, santa cruz (rn/rs), sao francisco, sao jose, sao raimundo. And \"penarol\"/\"river plate\" bare forms are the FOREIGN clubs (Libertadores), which I should curate as foreign clubs or leave fallback.\n\nSo the plan:\n1. Change `fallback_club` to use the base (UF-stripped) key as identity → merges \"luverdense mt\"/\"luverdense\" ✓.\n2. Curate the distinct-club groups so their state-suffixed keys resolve via registry before fallback: central_pe, central_sc, comercial_ms, comercial_pi, operario_ms, operario_mt, river_ac, river_pi, river_plate_se (Brazilian) — note \"river plate\" (ARG, Libertadores) stays fallback \"river plate\" ✓ distinct from \"river plate se\" after UF-strip?? WAIT — fallback base for \"River Plate - SE\" → strip SE → \"river plate\" == Libertadores \"River Plate\"! COLLISION. So river_plate_se MUST be curated (or fallback would merge them). Same for \"penarol\" — \"Penarol AM\" → base \"penarol\" == Libertadores \"Peñarol\" (URU) → collision → curate penarol_am.\n   - rio branco ac / es — no bare \"rio branco\" elsewhere? Libertadores? No Rio Branco in Lib. Both curated.\n   - santa cruz rn/rs — bare \"Santa Cruz\" never appears uncurated? Cup file has \"Santa Cruz - PE\" → curated santa_cruz ✓. santa_cruz_rn, santa_cruz_rs curate.\n   - sao francisco ac/pa, sao jose pa/rs, sao raimundo am/pa/rr — curate all.\n   - central pe/sc, comercial ms/pi, operario ms/mt, river ac/pi — curate all.\n   - \"vitoria es\"? earlier: \"Vitoria F. C. - ES\"/\"Vitoria ES\" → base \"vitoria f c\"/\"vitoria es\"... \"Vitoria ES\" → base \"vitoria\" → collides with curated vitoria (BA)!! Hmm — resolve order: registry first. \"Vitoria ES\" isn't a curated alias → tier2: base \"vitoria\" + uf ES → curated vitoria has state BA ≠ ES → None → fallback base \"vitoria\" → id \"x_vitoria\" == Vitória-BA fallback?? NO WAIT — Vitória-BA is CURATED, so raw \"Vitória - BA\" resolves to curated `vitoria` — fallback never applies. But \"Vitoria ES\" → fallback id \"x_vitoria\" — a NEW identity that doesn't equal curated vitoria ✓ distinct. Phew — curated clubs never go through fallback. But is \"x_vitoria\" (ES) distinct from... any other club with base \"vitoria\"? \"EC Vitoria\" (BRF) → is \"ec vitoria\" a curated alias? YES (vitoria BA aliases include \"ec vitoria\") ✓. So only the ES one lands in \"x_vitoria\". Distinct ✓.\n   - BUT WAIT — worse: fallback base of \"Atletico - ES\" → \"atletico\" → x_atletico. And \"Atletico - AC\"→\"x_atletico\", \"Atletico - BA\"→\"x_atletico\"?? I curated atletico_ac (\"atletico ac\", \"atletico acreano\") and atletico_alagoinhas (\"atletico ba\") ✓ but \"Atletico - ES\" not curated → x_atletico. Any other bare \"Atletico\"? No (Libertadores has bare \"Athletico\" → curated). So \"x_atletico\" = Atlético-ES alone ✓ fine.\n   - And CRITICAL: fallback for foreign \"Nacional (URU)\" → base \"nacional uru\" (URU not UF) ✓ stays distinct. \"Guaraní (PAR)\" ✓. \"Barcelona-EQU\" → \"barcelona equ\" ✓.\n   - Another: \"Botafogo PB\" curated ✓, \"Botafogo SP\" curated ✓. \"Moto Club de São Luís\" (BRF) vs Cup \"Moto Club - MA\": base \"moto club\" vs \"moto club de sao luis\" — DIFFERENT keys, same club! Collision list doesn't show it (moto club not in list since variants resolve differently... wait \"moto clube\" vs \"moto club\"...). Hmm: BRF \"Moto Club de São Luís\" and \"Moto Clube\" (6) and Cup \"Moto Club - MA\" (9) → keys \"moto club de sao luis\", \"moto clube\", \"moto club\" — three identities for (probably) the same club. Minor long-tail noise — curate? \"moto clube\" with aliases all three forms. OK I'll add it.\n   - \"Sport Boys\" (Peruvian) — no collision ✓.\n   - \"America de Cali\" vs FIFA \"América de Cali\"? fine.\n\n3. The bare-form + state-form same-club pairs (luverdense etc., ~70 of them) get unified by the base-key fallback ✓ — no curation needed.\n\nOne more check — fallback base collisions WITH CURATED bases: e.g. fallback base \"santos laguna\"? No UF. What about a fallback club whose base equals a curated alias but whose full key isn't curated? E.g. \"Guarani de Juazeiro\" → base \"guarani de juazeiro\" ≠ \"guarani\" ✓. \"Gremio Novorizontino\" ✓ distinct. \"Santa Cruz RN\"→ I'll curate. \"Sao Jose PA\"/\"RS\" → curate (else both → base \"sao jose\" merged WRONG). \"Uniao Rondonopolis\"... no collision.\n\nAlso fallback with parentheticals: \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\" — boavista is curated including the full paren form ✓. Other parenthetical raw names: \"River (PI)\" → key \"river pi\" → base \"river\" — RIVER-PI! I'm curating river_pi with alias \"river pi\" ✓ (also river_ac \"river ac\").\n\nOK — also \"tuntum EC\" → base \"tuntum ec\" fine.\n\nNow, there's one more important interplay: FIFA club matching uses exact fifa_names — unaffected by fallback changes ✓.\n\nAnd BASE_INDEX removal earlier — fine.\n\nNow implement:\n1. clubs.py: fallback_club uses base key for identity; add the distinct-club curations: central_pe, central_sc, comercial_ms, comercial_pi, operario_ms, operario_mt, river_ac, river_pi, river_plate_se, penarol_am, rio_branco_ac, rio_branco_es, santa_cruz_rn, santa_cruz_rs, sao_francisco_ac, sao_francisco_pa, sao_jose_pa, sao_jose_rs, sao_raimundo_am, sao_raimundo_pa, sao_raimundo_rr, moto_clube. \n   Hmm wait — also \"novorizontino\" (sp) vs \"gremio novorizontino\"? \"Novorizontino\" base = \"novorizontino\" — unifies \"Novorizontino\"/\"Novorizontino SP\"? \"Sao Jose PA\"... fine. Also \"gremio novorizontino\" distinct ✓.\n   Also note \"red bull brasil\"/\"red bull brasil sp\" unifies via base \"red bull brasil\" ✓ (same club).\n   \n2. Verify the alias-collision assert still passes (unique aliases across clubs).\n\n3. engine.py: rewrite _dedupe with preferred-source pairing-merge design + standings simplification + CBF tiebreaker (wins before GD).\n\nLet me also double-check \"river plate se\": Cup file \"River Plate - SE\"? From BR-Football: 'River AC' 24, and Cup 'River (PI)'... wait where's \"river plate se\" from? The collision list showed ('river plate', None), ('river plate se', 'SE'). Which file has \"River Plate - SE\"? Probably BR-Football Serie C (\"River Plate-SE\", a Sergipe club). And bare \"river plate\" from Libertadores. So river_plate_se must be curated with alias \"river plate se\" and maybe \"river plate se\"... and display \"River Plate-SE\". Hmm — careful: resolve \"River Plate\" (user query, meaning the Argentine club) → tier1: \"river plate\" not curated alias → tier2: no UF → fallback base \"river plate\" → x_river_plate (the Argentine club's matches) ✓. resolve \"River Plate-SE\" → \"river plate se\" → tier2: base \"river plate\" + UF SE → curated river_plate_se state SE == SE ✓ → river_plate_se. \n\nWait no — tier 1 checks \"river plate se\" in ALIAS_INDEX → curated ✓ directly. And tier 2 only matters for unlisted variants. OK.\n\nLet me now write all the club additions + fallback change, then rewrite engine dedupe.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6baad2001YFNFGn5PjimxYy","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b6b4728001L5wPBdAdSMRDKZ"}}
