tus\" → x_juventus ✓. From \"Paris Saint-Germain\" → x_paris_saint_germain ✓. Also the FIFA_CLUB_INDEX covers Brazilian ones ✓.\n\nImplementation: in build_knowledge_graph, accept a function to resolve FIFA club strings. Simpler: precompute in engine a `self._fifa_club_ids: dict[club_str, club_id]` for all distinct player clubs (Brazilian via FIFA_CLUB_INDEX, others via fallback_club(club_str).club_id), pass club_registry including those. But the club_registry built from match-file cache doesn't have FIFA-only clubs. Let me restructure: after loading players, extend a `self.clubs` registry with FIFA club fallbacks; the `plays_for` edge uses that.\n\nIn build_knowledge_graph, the club loop uses club_registry — I'll pass an extended registry from the engine. And players loop uses p.club_id — which is None for foreign clubs. Fix Player handling: keep club_id Brazilian-only but ALSO give the KG the raw club mapping. Cleaner: in engine._build_indexes, build `self._fifa_club_id: dict[str, str]` (raw club string → club_id) and pass a resolver to build_knowledge_graph... Let me just change build_knowledge_graph signature to take `fifa_club_map: dict[str, str]` and use it for plays_for edges + add those club nodes.\n\nAlso — while at it: `from_country` for clubs would be nice but skip.\n\nLet me implement:\n1. engine: build fifa_club_map = {club_str: club_id} for all distinct player.club values. For Brazilian → FIFA_CLUB_INDEX; else fallback_club(club_str).club_id (create Club objects, merge into self.clubs).\n2. knowledge_graph.build_knowledge_graph: add param fifa_club_map; in players loop, if p.club and mapped → plays_for edge.\n3. Also expose fifa club map for players search by foreign club (search_players club= param already does raw substring matching for foreign clubs ✓ no change needed).\n\nAlso fix the double-dash in team_profile.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6e0932001ar2mJd0tfW8ztQ","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b