rom_country]--> Alisson\n\nConnections between Neymar Jr and Paris Saint-Germain (max 3 hops):\n- Neymar Jr --[plays_for]--> Paris Saint-Germain\n- Neymar Jr --[from_country]--> Brazil --[~from_country]--> Thiago Silva --[plays_for]--> Paris Saint-Germain\n- Neymar Jr --[from_country]--> Brazil --[~from_country]--> Marquinhos --\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python - <<'EOF'\nfrom soccer_mcp.engine import SoccerData\nsd = SoccerData()\nprint(sd.graph_paths(\"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\")[\"summary\"][:400])\nprint()\nprint(sd.graph_paths(\"Neymar\", \"Alisson\")[\"summary\"][:400])\nprint()\nprint(sd.graph_paths(\"Neymar\", \"Paris Saint-Germain\")[\"summary\"][:300])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788240377037,"end":1788240377073}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The KG is now complete (17,966 plays_for edges for all players at all clubs). But graph_paths finds no connections within 3 hops — let me trace why:\n\nNeymar → PSG (plays_for, 1 hop) → other PSG players (2 hops) → their countries (3 hops) — and Palmeiras is reachable as: Neymar → country:Brazil (1 hop) → Brazilian players (2 hops) → their clubs e.g. Grêmio (3 hops) — but Palmeiras has no FIFA players! Palmeiras' neighbors are match nodes (2 hops away from club): Palmeiras → match → Flamengo... So Neymar→Brazil→players→clubs→(4 hops)→...→Palmeiras needs ≥5 hops realistically. 3 hops is too tight for club↔club connections via country hubs. Also — the country nodes are high-degree hubs (Brazil: 827+ players), and my `find_paths` has max_frontier=250 per node — with Brazil's 827 neighbors, frontier truncation might cut paths AND the visited_best logic prunes... Let me reconsider find_paths:\n\n```python\nqueue: deque[(node, trail)]\nvisited_best: dict node -> hops\nwhile queue and len(paths) < 10:\n    current, trail = queue.popleft()\n    if len(trail) >= max_hops: continue\n    frontier = 0\n    for rel, other in adj[current]:\n        frontier += 1\n        if frontier > max_frontier: break\n        step = trail + [(rel, other)]\n        if other == goal: paths.append(step); continue\n        hops = len(step)\n        if visited_best.get(other, 99) <= hops: continue\n        visited_best[other] = hops\n        queue.append((other, step))\n```\n\nThis is BFS with dedup — should find 3-hop paths if they exist: Flamengo → match (1) → club Boca? No — Flamengo and Boca never played each other in the data (they COULD have in Libertadores 2012-2021? Flamengo played Boca? No — Boca vs Brazilian teams: they played Corinthians 2012/2015? Lib data has Corinthians-Boca 2012 ✓. So Flamengo→match→??? For Flamengo→Boca: Flamengo →(1) any match →(2) any club in those matches (opponent) →(3) opponent's match... wait to REACH Boca in 3 hops: Flamengo →match→ club X → match2 → Boca — 4 hops. OR Flamengo →country Brazil? Flamengo node doesn't have a country edge (clubs only have state prop, no country edge). Hmm.\n\nSo club↔club typically = 2 hops if they played each other (club→match→club), or 4 if not. Player↔club: Neymar→PSG (1 hop if same club; for Palmeiras: Neymar→Brazil (1)→player (2)→club (3) — a Brazilian player at a Brazilian club! e.g. Neymar→country:Brazil→Ronaldo Cabrais (2)→Grêmio (3) ✓ 3 hops. For Palmeiras specifically: no FIFA squad → no player→Palmeiras edge → Neymar can't reach Palmeiras in 3. That's a true statement about the graph (they only connect via match nodes at 5 hops: Neymar→Brazil→player→club→match→Palmeiras... e.g. player at Grêmio→match→Palmeiras (4)? Neymar(1)→country:Brazil(2)→Ronaldo Cabrais(3)→Grêmio(4)→match(5)→Palmeiras. Yeah 5-6 hops.\n\nSo the paths tool with default max_hops=3 works for directly-related entities (Flamengo↔Fluminense 2 hops ✓, Neymar↔PSG 1 hop, Neymar↔Alisson 2 hops via Brazil country ✓). For distant pairs, increase max_hops. The BFS frontier cap 250 might bite on hub nodes (Brazil 827 neighbors) — paths through truncated neighbors get missed, fine for bounded responses.\n\nLet me test graph_paths(\"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\") (2 hops via Fla-Flu matches) and (\"Neymar\", \"Alisson\") (2 hops via country). And bump default max_hops for the MCP tool to 4 (bounded by frontier caps + 10 paths). Actually let me also make find_paths smarter: prioritize... no, keep simple. Just verify the close pairs work.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6eafc4001KQH60y1KoY0NPu","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b6e6b4a001Umx0MWr6Tm3D9k"}}
