ormalize_text(m.stage)): continue` — should filter. Wait the output shows \"13 match(es) found\" including non-finals — so stage filtering failed?? stage=\"final\", stage_key=\"final\". m.stage for these = \"semifinals\" — \"final\" in \"semifinals\" → TRUE (substring!). \"quarterfinals\" contains \"final\" too! Classic substring bug.\n\nFix: stage matching should be smarter — exact match OR word-boundary. Use exact match on normalized stage, else fallback to... The stage values: \"group stage\", \"round of 16\", \"quarterfinals\", \"semifinals\", \"final\". If user passes \"final\" they mean stage == \"final\". If they pass \"semi\" they probably mean semifinals. I'll implement: exact match first; if no exact matches, substring with word boundary check. Simplest robust: `stage_key == normalize_text(m.stage) or stage_key in tokens` where tokens = normalized stage split. \"final\" in [\"quarterfinals\"]? token is \"quarterfinals\" ≠ \"final\" ✓. \"group\" in [\"group\",\"stage\"] ✓. \"semifinal\"? token \"semifinals\" ≠ \"semifinal\" ✗ hmm — user typing \"semifinal\" wouldn't match token \"semifinals\". Add prefix matching on tokens: any(tok.startswith(stage_key) or stage_key.startswith(tok) for tok in tokens)? \"final\".startswith? tokens \"quarterfinals\".startswith(\"final\") = False ✓; \"final\" == \"final\" ✓ exact. \"semi\" → \"semifinals\".startswith(\"semi\") ✓. \"quarter\" → \"quarterfinals\".startswith(\"quarter\") ✓. \"16\" → tokens [\"round\",\"of\",\"16\"]: \"16\" == \"16\" ✓ exact token match. \n\nRule: match if stage_key equals a token OR a token startswith stage_key (min length 3 to avoid junk). Let me also handle \"round 5\" style: stage for Brasileirao is \"Round 22\" — user may search stage=\"Round 22\" → normalize \"round 22\", tokens match exact ✓.\n\nAlso — the biggest_wins as_dict doesn't include goal_margin — that's fine, tests can recompute. Actually let me add margin to output for usefulness: in biggest_wins include \"margin\". The Match.as_dict doesn't have margin; I'll add goal_margin to as_dict? It's useful generally. Add \"goal_margin\" when played.\n\nLet me fix the stage filter now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6fcf79001BaQdcAYgwBBpm1","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b6faae4001CWhgB4gNFrjWeG"}}
