nse\" → same base \"luverdense\" → same id ✓.\n\nThen in resolve_team:\n```python\nclub = resolve_club(query)\nif club is None:\n    key = normalize_text(query)\n    observed = self._observed_alias.get(key)\n    if observed is not None:\n        return observed, []\n```\nWait but careful — self._observed_alias values are Club objects from self.clubs (both curated and fallback). For curated ones resolve_club already handles. Fine.\n\nAlso for `_require_team` — works via resolve_team ✓.\n\nAlso `search_matches` calls `resolve_club(team)` directly after _require_team — that returns None for foreign clubs!! Let me look: `team_id = resolve_club(team).club_id if team else None`. For \"Boca Juniors\" — _require_team passes (after fix C), but then resolve_club returns None → crash! I must change search_matches (and other methods that call resolve_club after _require_team) to use a resolution helper that includes observed aliases. Let me refactor: engine gets `self._resolve(query) -> Optional[Club]` = resolve_club OR observed_alias exact. All internal uses switch to that.\n\nMethods calling resolve_club on user input: search_matches (team & opponent), head_to_head (a & b), team_stats, team_profile, team_graph. Replace all with self._resolve().\n\nLet me apply all fixes now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b745d20001pOL2sP00DPLbUy","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","messageID":"msg_05b742b8200196shSWtFYQZPYp"}}
