{"type":"text","timestamp":1788240947665,"sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","part":{"id":"prt_05b775de1001LDVGkXWKgQNjFL","messageID":"msg_05b7748b9001o4yuYENzBzvo8Y","sessionID":"ses_fa4a24ca1ffeh7JKx4QpKQV4BC","type":"text","text":"Complete. All 155 tests pass and lint is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP Server** per `TASK.md`:\n\n- **`server.py`** — MCP stdio server (mcp 2.x SDK) with **19 tools** covering all five spec categories: match queries, team queries, player queries, competition queries, statistical analysis, plus a knowledge-graph interface (`graph_overview`, `team_graph`, `graph_paths`). Verified end-to-end with a real JSON-RPC round-trip (initialize → tools/list → tools/call).\n\n- **`soccer_mcp/`** package — models, normalization, a curated club registry (~120 clubs, ~400 alias forms), CSV loaders for all 6 files, an in-memory property graph (36k nodes / 98k edges), and the query engine.\n\n**Key engineering decisions:**\n- **Cross-file reconciliation**: the 5 match files overlap heavily with conflicting dates (±1 day shifts in BR-Football) and mislabelled rows. Per (competition, season), the family-specific Kaggle file is authoritative; BR-Football rows merge by pairing (contributing corners/shots stats and filling 81 missing 2022 scores); 173 mislabelled rows dropped → 16,712 clean matches.\n- **Team-name normalization**: layered resolution handles \"Palmeiras-SP\" / \"SE Palmeiras\" / \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" / bare \"Athletico\" (Libertadores), keeps Flamengo-RJ vs Flamengo-PI distinct, unifies \"Luverdense-MT\"/\"Luverdense\", and gives typo tolerance with candidate suggestions.\n\n**Verification against spec:**\n- 2019 Série A standings reproduce the spec's example exactly (Flamengo 90 pts, 28W 6D 4L; Santos 2nd with 22 wins); champions 2003–2022 all match history.\n- **Tests**: 35 BDD Gherkin scenarios (pytest-bdd) + GWT pytest modules + 28 sample questions answered through MCP tools + stdio transport test — **155 tests, 94% coverage**.\n- Performance criteria asserted in tests: simple lookups < 2s, aggregates < 5s.","time":{"start":1788240944609,"end":1788240947654}}}
